{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports"]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncQueue","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO"},{"text":"> { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reports wait, without a bound, until they are read, so none is missed by reading late."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Drops are rare (each is a whole segment, or bytes recovery couldn’t read), so they don’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pile up. The sequence ends once the store is gone and every report has been read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One task reads the reports at a time. The first iterator to read holds them until its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iteration ends or it is released; a second reader meanwhile waits its turn, logging a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"warning once, then reads on from the next report, so the first gets every report in order.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A reader cancelled while it waits returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text